Real defects:

- P1 — A repository-controlled test can replace the reviewer executable with a fake wrapper that restores the original before exiting. The code hashes the executable before the test and only again after the reviewer finishes; both hashes therefore match. It also fingerprints only the first command token, missing scripts invoked through `python`, `sh`, `env`, etc. This permits an L2 change to fabricate a passing review and reach `SAFE TO MERGE`. See [bin/coverloop:2433](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2433), [bin/coverloop:2458](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2458), [bin/coverloop:2683](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2683), and [bin/coverloop:2722](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2722). Reviewers must run before repository-controlled tests or from an immutable execution snapshot.

- P1 — `check` exposes the raw diff to arbitrary reviewer commands without applying the existing secret egress scan. Redaction happens only after reviewer execution, when capturing output, so a committed credential can already have reached an external model. See [bin/coverloop:2614](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2614), [bin/coverloop:2625](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2625), and [bin/coverloop:1000](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:1000). Known secret-bearing packets must stop before any reviewer process starts.

Non-blocking correctness/documentation defects:

- The documented GLM reviewer command runs `git diff` from the scratch directory where `check` deliberately executes reviewers, so the example cannot obtain the repository diff. It should consume `$COVERLOOP_DIFF`. See [README.md:169](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/README.md:169) and [docs/GATE.md:47](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/docs/GATE.md:47).

- The changelog and central code comment still claim verification-only evidence advances the baseline, contradicting the shipped full-authorization behavior documented later. See [CHANGELOG.md:22](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/CHANGELOG.md:22), [CHANGELOG.md:63](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/CHANGELOG.md:63), and [bin/coverloop:1657](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:1657).

