    39	    # not begin a `-----` marker run. A real PEM body (base64 + whitespace, plus
    40	    # `Proc-Type:`/`DEK-Info:` headers on encrypted keys) never contains five
    41	    # consecutive dashes, so this matches every real key, but a BEGIN can no
    42	    # longer scan ACROSS the next marker: thousands of bare `-----BEGIN` markers
    43	    # (with or without a distant END) each fail in O(1). Because the tempered dot
    44	    # ALREADY bounds the scan at the next marker, the span is UNBOUNDED on
