    59	    # Leading `\b` is the ReDoS guard AND the whole guarantee: a secret name
    60	    # starts at a word boundary, and a long word-char run (the attack input) has
    61	    # NO interior boundaries, so re.search skips those millions of offsets in
    62	    # O(1) instead of re-expanding the variable prefix at each. With `\b` in
    63	    # place the prefix `*` backtracks only at the O(1) run-start boundaries, so
    64	    # the pattern is linear even UNBOUNDED (measured: 2 MB adversarial input
    65	    # ~0.1s). The prefix is therefore left unbounded on purpose: a `{0,N}` cap
    66	    # would silently stop redacting a name whose prefix exceeds N (Sol/GLM R2
    67	    # caught `A*65 + _KEY=[REDACTED:secret-value] leaking under a {0,64} cap) — a real
    68	    # secret-leak regression — while buying no ReDoS safety `\b` doesn't already
    69	    # give. Without `\b`, unbounded `*` before a required suffix is O(n^2) and
