   139	# (over-redacting a transcript is safe; over-blocking an egress packet breaks legitimate reviews).
   140	#
   141	# The clean model (Sol r1-r9 converged): a secret-family assignment is CLEAN only when it is
   142	# unambiguously code carrying a benign value; anything that reads as a config/env/YAML dump line, or
   143	# carries an opaque literal, BLOCKS.
   144	#   * `=` form (env/config dumps -- the rule's original target)                         -> BLOCK.
   145	#   * value is EXACTLY a [REDACTED:<label>] marker (scan-of-redact idempotency)          -> CLEAN.
   146	#   * CODE-STRUCTURED line (a code-punctuation char ,;(){}[]=<>`|& at/after the value): the line is
   147	#     lexed once (parity-aware string lexer; escaped quotes never open/close; unterminated literal
   148	#     runs to EOL). BLOCK iff a string literal with >= 8 chars of non-marker content, or a >=16
   149	#     opaque bareword that is NOT a pure-identifier key/call, appears at/after the value start.
   150	#     Benign code values (bool/null, short literals, identifiers, calls) stay CLEAN.
   151	#   * NON-code line (no code punctuation after the value = a YAML/env/prose plain line): the value is
   152	#     the REST of the line (and a plain scalar may fold onto the immediately-following more-indented
   153	#     line -- YAML forbids a blank line inside a plain scalar, so only the next line matters). CLEAN
   154	#     only if that whole remaining value is a lone bool/null with no fold; otherwise BLOCK (fail
   155	#     closed -- this is where env dumps, multiword passphrases, opaque tokens, colon-bearing scalars
   156	#     and folds all live).
   157	# RESIDUAL (documented, OPERATOR DECISION — a real strictness trade, not a fixable defect):
   158	# scan() no longer catches an UNQUOTED pure-identifier-shaped value/key
   159	# (`[A-Za-z0-9_$]+`, any length) on a code-punctuation-bearing line is structurally identical to a
   160	# legitimate identifier -- a variable ref (`currentAccessToken`), a type name (`AuthenticationToken`),
